From d837d9b0e35f4e63146fbaa8cb8cceed75a2eff5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:04:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Split Start Day from shop check-in; move dashboard CTA into
 header
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Start Day is now its own step: a rep can start their day anywhere (no
geofence), confirmed with a photo of their bike/vehicle's meter reading,
once per (IST) calendar day. Checking in at a shop stays geofenced to
100m but no longer needs its own photo — a rep must have started their
day first, or they're prompted to.

- New sales_day_starts table + get_my_day_start()/start_day() RPCs;
  start_dealer_visit() drops its photo param and gains the day-started
  gate (drop-then-recreate since the signature changes).
- New StartDay.jsx screen (GPS + mandatory meter photo, no geofence).
- CheckIn.jsx: dealer list only, tap-to-confirm, no photo step; blocks
  with a "start your day first" prompt if today's day isn't started.
- DealerDetail.jsx: same day-started guard on its inline check-in;
  duty-on photo capture removed from check-in.
- visitMedia.js: uploadVisitMedia's dealerId param generalized to
  folder, since day-start photos aren't tied to a dealer.
- SalesDashboard.jsx: the Check In/Start Day button now lives inside
  the purple header (was straddling the header/content boundary,
  creating a purple-on-purple overlap seam) and branches three ways —
  Start Day, Check In at a Shop, or the existing "checked in" banner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxWPdEf21EL6SvRpGBbX8q
